
In this repository you will fine a project that 

 * obisdian plugin written in js/ts 
 * the plugin extracts recipes from different websites 
 * it translates those recipes into obisdian markdown files 


MPORTANT - DO NOT COMMIT CHANGES UNLESS ASKED TO 


 * use the ./references folder for new git repositories  
 * you have the obsidian cli to help with debugging errors 

## Issue tracking 

When you are in PLAN  and you have a finsihed and refined a plan i want you store the plan in an issue  along with the todo list 

The file convention is the following . .EPICS/<000N>-<epic title>/ISSUES/000N-[title of issue].md  and the issue numbers increment by 1 


***IMPORTANT*** - IN PLAN MODE ALWAYS ASK USER WHAT EPIC YOU ARE WORKING ON 


TESTS

 When you are testing copy the tests to ISSUES/ the issues number / test/ test data and test commaands  
